WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.538
Switches can be managed or unmanaged. Simply put, a managed switch is one that can be configured.

00:07.538 --> 00:15.205
It can have an IP address set, it can have security settings enabled, and it will usually support VLANs.

00:15.205 --> 00:26.577
An unmanaged switch, on the other hand, is also known as a plug and play switch because that is basically all you do with it. You plug it in, you plug devices into it, and that is it.

00:26.577 --> 00:37.762
There is no configuration to set up. For the exam, know that managed switches are configurable and unmanaged switches are not configurable.

